@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Deactivate or reactivate account
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
actor "Administrator" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "AccountStatusDialog /\nAccountStatusForm" as page
  participant "IAccountService / AccountService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "AccountsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ChangeAccountStatusCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "DesignatedAdministratorPolicy / UserAccount" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "IAuditEventWriter" as audit
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
== Open: the form reads its account ==
actor -> page : Choose Deactivate or Reactivate on a row or the details page; the dialog receives the account ID and the requested status
page -> client : accountResource(GetAccountQuery { id }); the action stays disabled while it loads (loading)
client -> access : GET /api/accounts/{id}, with the checks and handler of Read account details
access --> client : 200 AccountDetail, 404, or a failure
alt Account read
  client --> page : The dialog names the account with its email and role; Deactivate account or Reactivate account enabled
else Read failed: 500 or no response
  client --> page : load-failed: alert with Try again (reload()), plus the reference ID when a 500 carried one; Cancel closes; the action stays disabled
else 404
  client --> page : Form emits notFound; the dialog closes with NotFound; the owning page increments its counter: the details page shows its not-found state with Back to accounts, and the directory shows the "Account not found" toast
end
== Submit ==
actor -> page : Confirm Deactivate or Reactivate (dialog names the account)
page -> page : Disable both buttons; show progress; draftChange reports pending
page -> client : changeStatus(ChangeAccountStatusCommand: id, active, expectedVersion from the form's accountResource)
client -> access : PUT /api/accounts/{id}/status
alt No response: the connection dropped or the request timed out
  client --> page : changeStatus() rejects with a no-response error; the change may or may not have been made
  page -> page : AccountStatusForm emits unconfirmed (DraftState.unconfirmed until settled), which the dialog relays while it stays open; the owning page increments its counter at once, so the page behind rereads; keep both buttons disabled while the account is read again, so focus moves to the alert
  page -> client : AccountStatusForm calls reload() on its accountResource once (GET /api/accounts/{id})
  client --> page : Latest account details and version
  alt The account already has the requested status
    page --> actor : The change is in place: the form emits changed; the dialog closes with Changed(account) and the toast names the account and result
  else Status unchanged
    page --> actor : failed presentation with "We couldn't confirm the deactivation"; no reference ID; the action resends with the reloaded version only when chosen (a stale 409 on that repeat leaves out "Nothing was changed"); Cancel closes with no result, since the page behind already reread
  end
else Response received
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry (zero clock skew)
access -> db : LoadAccountAccessAsync: current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; inactive or missing account; credential version changed
  access -> audit : AppendRestrictedAsync(Denied); no payload
  access --> client : 401
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor: end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401; login opens (session-ended); nothing changed
else Authenticated Collaborator (profile P: no accounts.manage)
  access -> audit : AppendRestrictedAsync(Denied); no payload
  access --> client : 403
  client --> page : refreshCapabilities() (deduplicated); AccountStatusForm emits forbidden; the dialog closes with Forbidden and the owning page calls showStatus(AccessDenied); nothing changed
else Administrator
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send ChangeAccountStatusCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : Validate identifier, active flag and expectedVersion
  alt Invalid request
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; no business mutation
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Keep the dialog open; show the API's message without Try again or a reference ID, since a resubmission would be refused again; nothing changed
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle ChangeAccountStatusCommand
    handler -> db : Load account by ID
    db --> handler : Current account or none
    alt Account missing
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : NotFound ProblemDetails
      client --> page : Form emits notFound; the dialog closes with NotFound; the owning page increments its counter: the details page shows its not-found state with Back to accounts, and the directory shows the "Account not found" toast
    else Account found
      handler -> entity : L2-008 reject deactivation of the designated administrator -> 409
      entity --> handler : Allowed or protected
      alt Designated account and active = false
        handler -> audit : AppendRestrictedAsync(Rejected), outside any business transaction (L2-039.2)
        audit -> db : Insert audit event only
        handler --> ctrl : 409 protected-identity with explanation; account stays active
        ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails (protected-identity)
        client --> page : blocked state: the explanation (the designated administrator must stay active) fills the alert region and becomes the dialog description; Close only, no retry; focus moves to Close; the form emits outdated, so Close returns Outdated and the page rereads
      else Stored version differs from expectedVersion
        handler --> ctrl : 409 stale version; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails (stale)
        client --> page : Promise rejects with the stale 409
        page -> client : AccountStatusForm emits outdated and calls reload() on its accountResource once (GET /api/accounts/{id}, authorized as above)
        client --> page : Latest account details and version
        page --> actor : stale state: the explanation fills the alert region and becomes the dialog description; focus moves to Review account; nothing changed; no resubmission; Review account emits reviewRequested: the dialog closes with Review, and AccountsPage navigates to /accounts/:id while AccountDetailPage increments its counter; Cancel returns Outdated
      else Permitted change at current version
        handler -> entity : L2-004 set active flag; password, role and assignments kept
        entity --> handler : Updated account
        handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent(success); SaveChangesAsync updates where version matches and commits both
        alt Racing save changed the version
          db --> handler : 0 rows; roll back update and audit
          handler --> ctrl : 409 stale version, handled as above
          ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails (stale)
          client --> page : Same handling as the stale branch above
        else Commit fails unexpectedly
          db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
          handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
          ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-save claim
          client --> page : failed state: nothing changed; reference ID; Try again repeats the request (a busy 503 is shown the same way)
        else Commit succeeds
          db --> handler : New committed version
          handler --> ctrl : 200 with safe account summary and version
          ctrl --> client : Success response
          client --> page : Form emits changed; the dialog closes with Changed(account); the owning page increments its counter and shows the "Account deactivated" or "Account reactivated" toast naming the account
          page --> actor : Deactivated account's tokens return 401 on their next request (L2-002.3)
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
end
note over ctrl, db
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
